  "question": {
    "text": "The total number of 'Sigma' and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Pi</mi></math> bonds in 2-formylhex-4-enoic acid is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "22",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A single bond is a result of the axial overlap of bonding orbitals. Hence, it contributes a sigma bond. A multiple bond (double or triple bond) contain one sigma bond and the remaining are pi bonds. </p><p>The total number of sigma and pi bond in </p><p> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>-Formyl hex-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>-enoic acid is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22</mn></math>.</p><p>The compound can be represented as,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/9639a590-3ced-4c0b-a78e-b131b0817888.png\" style=\"width: 482px; height: 206px;\"/></p>",
